 "about_text": "Patricia Sweetow Gallery is a contemporary art gallery that opened in San Francisco in 1997 and relocated to Downtown Los Angeles in 2022, where it now operates from South Santa Fe Avenue. The gallery is led by principal Patricia Sweetow with associate director Christal Darling. Its program centers on artists working in non-traditional materials—textile, ceramic, fiber, and craft-based practices—that challenge institutional hierarchies between 'high' and 'low' art. Exhibiting artists often draw on craft traditions to interrogate colonial structures, personal identity, and cultural memory. The gallery has participated in numerous art fairs across the U.S. and Canada and represents a roster of emerging and mid-career artists working across sculpture, painting, ceramics, and fiber art.",
